  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="block__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Principles</p>
      <h2 id="principles-title">How I think the work should be done.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="rows">
      <li><strong>The number needs an owner.</strong> <span>Someone has to be able to explain it and answer for it. That is a person, never a tool.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Evidence first.</strong> <span>If I can't show where a figure came from, I don't have a figure.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Reconcile before you report.</strong> <span>A report built on an unreconciled balance is an opinion with formatting.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Explain the movement.</strong> <span>The balance matters less than why it changed since last time.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Write it down.</strong> <span>A procedure that lives in one head cannot be checked or handed over.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="block__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The bonus</p>
      <h2 id="tools-title">Software and AI, in support.</h2>
      <p class="lead">I also write code. It doesn't replace the accounting. It removes the repetition around it.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="rows">
      <li><strong>Accounting systems</strong> <span>Xero and MYOB, including migration between them.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Analysis and reporting</strong> <span>Excel with Power Query and Power Pivot, Power BI, SQL.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Automation</strong> <span>Python, Power Automate and accounting APIs for the work that repeats.</span></li>
      <li><strong>AI</strong> <span>Agents and reusable procedures for preparation and first drafts, with a person reviewing and signing.</span></li>
    </ul>
